n&gt;To maintain visual clarity, Foreign Keys (FK) are not explicitly listed in the child table boxes. Instead, the arrows represent the requirement for the Child table to store the Primary Key (ID) of the Parent table to establish the relational link.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontColor=default;" parent="WIyWlLk6GJQsqaUBKTNV-1" vertex="1">
